          %h2#references References
          %div
            %h3#early_references_on_cohomology Early references on (co)homology
            %p
              The original references on
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
              in the form of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+cohomology"} cellular cohomology
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Kolmogoroff"}> Andrei Kolmogoroff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Über die Dualität im Aufbau der kombinatorischen Topologie
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://mi.mathnet.ru/msb5361"} mathnet
            %p
              A footnote on the first page reads as follows, giving attribution to
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Alexander35a"} Alexander 35a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a{:href => "#Alexander35a"} 35b
            %blockquote
              %p
                Die Resultate dieser Arbeit wurden für den Fall gewöhnlicher Komplexe vom Verfasser im Frühling und im Sommer 1934 erhalten und teilweise an der Internationalen Konferenz für Tensoranalysis (Moskau) im Mai 1934 vorgetragen. Die hier dargestellte allgemeinere Theorie bildete den Gegenstand eines Vortrages, den der Verfasser an der Internationalen Topologischen Konferenz (Moskau, September 1935) hielt; bei letzterer Gelegenheit erfuhr er, dass ein grosser Teil dieser Resultate im Falle von Komplexen indessen von Herrn Alexander erhalten worden ist. Vgl. die inzwischen erschienenen Noten von Herrn
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+W.+Alexander"} Alexander
                in den «Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences U.S.A.», 21, (1935), 509—512. Herr Alexander trug über seine Resultate ebenfalls an der Moskauer Topologischen Konferenz vor. Verallgemeinerungen für abgeschlossene Mengen und die Konstruktion eines Homologieringes für Komplexe und abgeschlossene Mengen, über welche der Verfasser ebenso an der Tensorkonferenz 1934 vorgetragen hat, werden in einer weiteren Publikation dargestellt. Diese weitere Begriffsbildungen sind übrigens ebenfalls von Herrn Alexander gefunden und teilweise in den erwähnten Noten publiziert.
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Kolmogoroff"}> Andrei Kolmogoroff
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Homologiering des Komplexes und des lokal-bicompakten Raumes
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "http://mi.mathnet.ru/msb5475"} mathnet
              %li#Alexander35a
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+W.+Alexander"}> J. W. Alexander
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On the chains of a complex and their duals
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.21.8.50"} doi:10.1073/pnas.21.8.50
              %li#Alexander35b
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+W.+Alexander"}> J. W. Alexander
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On the ring of a compact metric space
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.21.8.511"} doi:10.1073/pnas.21.8.511
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+W.+Alexander"}> J. W. Alexander
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On the connectivity ring of an abstract space
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1968484"} doi:10.2307/1968484
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/alexcon.pdf"} pdf
            %p
              The term “cohomology” was introduced by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hassler+Whitney"} Hassler Whitney
              in
            %ul
              %li#Whitney37
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hassler+Whitney"}> Hassler Whitney
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em On matrices of integers and combinatorial topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/duke-mathematical-journal/volume-3/issue-1/On-matrices-of-integers-and-combinatorial-topology/10.1215/S0012-7094-37-00304-1.short"} doi:10.1215/S0012-7094-37-00304-1
            %p See also
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hassler+Whitney"}> Hassler Whitney
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On products in a complex
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1968795"} doi:10.2307/1968795
            %p
              The notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
              is due to
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"}> Samuel Eilenberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Singular homology theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/1969185"} doi:10.2307/1969185
            %p
              The notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+cohomology"} monadic cohomology
              via
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+resolutions"} canonical resolutions
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jon+Beck"} Jon Beck
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Homology and Standard Constructions
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seminar+on+Triples+and+Categorical+Homology+Theory"} Seminar on Triples and Categorical Homology Theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %strong 80
                  %strong 18
                  (2008) 186-248 [
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/18/tr18abs.html"}> tac:18
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/18/tr18.pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Cartan-Eilenberg cohomology and triples
                  %strong 112
                  3 (1996) 219–238 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(95)00138-7"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(95)00138-7
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.math.mcgill.ca/barr/papers/coho.pdf"} pdf
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Barr-CECohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Algebraic cohomology: the early days
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Galois Theory, Hopf Algebras, and Semiabelian Categories
                  %strong 43
                  (2004) 1–26 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/fic/043"}> doi:10.1090/fic/043
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.math.mcgill.ca/barr/papers/algcohom.pdf"} pdf
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Barr-AlgebraicCohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %p
              The general abstract perspective on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
              (subsuming
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+cohomology"} sheaf cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercohomology"} hypercohomology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+cohomology"} non-abelian cohomology
              and indications of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology"} Whitehead-generalized cohomology
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kenneth+Brown"}> Kenneth Brown
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BrownAHT"} Abstract homotopy theory and generalized sheaf cohomology
                (1973)
          %h3#general_2 General
          %p Textbook accounts:
